    "explanation": "This dispute turns on POL-NS-21 and POL-NS-22. The trip was on-demand (trip_record.scheduled_at is null), so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from the driver's arrival. The platform trip record (EV-TRIP-05054) fixes that arrival at 09:47:05 and the end of the free wait at 09:52:05; the driver-device GPS trace (EV-GPS-05054) corroborates it — its nearest fix is 2.73 m from the pickup, well inside POL-NS-21's 50 m arrival radius, and its fixes show the vehicle stationary from 09:46:50 to the last fix at 09:51:20. The driver cancelled at 09:51:25, 260 seconds after arriving and 40 seconds before the free wait expired; the trip record's own derived field cancelled_after_free_wait is false. POL-NS-22 authorises the 5.00 SGD no-show fee only when the driver cancels AFTER the free wait. That condition was not satisfied, so the 5.00 SGD line on EV-FARE-05054 (total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is not chargeable. The whole contested amount is returned: FULL_REFUND of 5.00 SGD.\n\nTo the driver: your contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met in full — two in-app messages (09:47:30 and 09:49:50, both read) and one in-app call (09:50:30, unanswered, 22 s), all before the 09:51:25 cancellation — and your advocate was right to concede it. But POL-NS-23 only opens a route to void a fee; it does not create one, so your claim that the fee should stand and be paid to you as DRIVER_COMPENSATION is rejected. Your statement that you 'waited more than 5 minutes' is not borne out: the record puts the wait at 260 seconds (40 s short of the 300 s), the trace carries 22 fixes at a 30 s interval with no gap in which further waiting could hide (max gap 30 s), and your own advocate accepted the arithmetic. The rider's failure to come down does not change the result, because a no-show cancellation is only valid once the free wait has run.\n\nTo the rider: you are right, and the 5.00 SGD is refunded. Your reading of the 5-minute wait is correct on this record.\n\nNo driver compensation arises: POL-NS-22 transfers the fee to the driver only where the fee is chargeable, and it is not. No referral is produced: the amount charged was exactly the policy's 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not fire; POL-NS-24's goodwill credit requires a failed arrival, which did not occur; and POL-NS-25's counter (rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d) is not present on this profile. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05054-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and nothing needed turns on it, so POL-GEN-26's escalation for an unprovable fact is not engaged. The dispute value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's first band, where POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final. Confidence 0.95, resting on the complete weight-1.0 trip record and GPS trace that carry the deciding facts."
